  "verbalization": "Candesartan is closely related to Forasartan through a shared structural similarity, which is reflected in their high similarity scores in the dataset. Both Candesartan and Forasartan bind to Agtr1, a key receptor in the renin-angiotensin system, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving the angiotensin II receptor. The lowest common ancestors of these entities point to the broader class of angiotensin II receptor antagonists, reinforcing the connection between Candesartan and Agtr1. The evidence suggests that Candesartan may act through a mechanism similar to Forasartan, which in turn binds to Agtr1. This relationship is further supported by the shared structural features and the binding of related compounds to the receptor. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of the angiotensin II receptor in the pharmacological action of these drugs, with Candesartan potentially functioning through a similar mechanism to its structural relatives.",
